# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/pools/internships.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event intern_midsummer_review
# en: The Midsummer Review
title [9f057d] = 仲夏评估
# en: {Halfway through the placement, your supervisor asks to see you. There's a single sheet of notes on the desk, face down.|The midsummer review again: the desk, the sheet, the tea nobody drinks.|You know the review's shape by now. You still don't know what's on the sheet.} {performance(internship) >= 60: Your supervisor is almost smiling.|{performance(internship) < 40: Your supervisor is not smiling.|Your supervisor's face gives nothing away.}}
text [e7c69e] = {实习过半，主管叫你过去。桌上有一张笔记，扣着放。|又是仲夏评估：那张桌子，那张纸，那杯没人喝的茶。|你现在熟悉评估的套路了。你仍然不知道那张纸上写了什么。}{performance(internship) >= 60: 你的主管几乎在微笑。|{performance(internship) < 40: 你的主管没有笑。|你的主管面无表情。}}
# en: A supervisor's desk with a single sheet of notes face down, a student sitting opposite with hands folded too tightly.
scene [cda6e8] = 主管的桌上扣着一张笔记，一个学生坐在对面，双手握得太紧。
# en: Ask for honest criticism
opt.left.label [7e14a3] = 请对方直言批评
# en: {You get it, three things you do badly, in order. You fix two of them by the end of the summer. Your supervisor notices both.|"Most interns ask for praise," your supervisor says, and turns the sheet over. It's a long list. You're grateful for every line, eventually.|This time you ask to see the sheet itself. It's shorter than you feared, and every line is fair.}
opt.left.say.1 [22ee92] = {你得到了：你做得不好的三件事，按顺序排列。到夏天结束时你改掉了两件。你的主管两件都注意到了。|“大多数实习生要的是表扬，”你的主管说着，把纸翻了过来。清单很长。最终你对每一行都心存感激。|这一次你要求看那张纸本身。它比你担心的短，每一行都很公道。}
# en: Ask what you've done well
opt.right.label [d826f5] = 问问自己哪里做得好
# en: {Your supervisor reads the good half aloud. You leave glowing, and never hear the other half.|"Your handwriting," your supervisor says, after a pause, "is excellent." You decide to take it.|Your supervisor reads you the top of the sheet and folds the rest away. You'll wonder what's under the fold.}
opt.right.say.1 [5452ea] = {你的主管把好的那一半念了出来。你满面春风地离开，再也没听到另一半。|“你的字，”你的主管顿了一下说，“写得非常好。”你决定接受这句话。|你的主管给你念了纸的上半截，把剩下的折了起来。你会一直好奇折痕底下写了什么。}

@event intern_credit_taken
# en: Someone Else's Name
title [737ae1] = 别人的名字
# en: {The report you spent a week on is pinned up in the corridor, praised by everyone, with another intern's name at the bottom.|Another piece of your work, another name on it.|It's happened again, and this time the other intern doesn't even look away.} {Your supervisor is reading it with approval.|The other intern is being congratulated.|Your notes are still on your desk, in your hand.}
text [eb5b31] = {你花了一个星期写的报告钉在走廊里，人人称赞，署名却是另一个实习生。|又一份你的成果，又一个别人的名字。|又发生了，这一次那个实习生连目光都不躲了。}{你的主管正赞许地读着它。|那个实习生正接受大家的祝贺。|你的笔记还在你桌上，是你的笔迹。}
# en: A report pinned on a wall, a student staring at the name at the bottom of it, which is not their own.
scene [27205c] = 一份钉在墙上的报告，一个学生盯着报告底部的名字，那不是他自己的。
# en: Take it to your supervisor
opt.left.label [13030f] = 找你的主管
# en: {You bring your notes, your drafts, your dates. Your supervisor reads them in silence and changes the name in red ink. The corridor goes very quiet around you.|You make your case calmly. The name is changed. The other intern doesn't speak to you again, which is fine.|You put your notes on your supervisor's desk, in your hand and dated. The name is changed, and this time the other intern looks away.}
opt.left.say.1 [399e9e] = {你带上笔记、草稿和日期。主管默默读完，用红墨水改了名字。你周围的走廊一下子安静了。|你冷静地陈述理由。名字改了。那个实习生再也没和你说过话，这样也好。|你把笔记放在主管桌上，你的笔迹，注明了日期。名字改了，这一次，那个实习生移开了目光。}
# en: {Your supervisor hears you out and says it's "a matter for the two of you". It isn't. You go back to your desk with your face burning.|Without proof enough, you sound petty, and you know it. The name stays.|Your notes are in your hand, but so, it turns out, is a draft in theirs. Your supervisor can't tell which came first, and the name stays.}
opt.left.say.2 [974ec6] = {主管听你说完，说这是“你们俩之间的事”。不是的。你回到桌前，脸上火辣辣的。|证据不够，你显得斤斤计较，你自己也知道。名字没改。|你的笔记是你的笔迹，可结果对方也有一份自己笔迹的草稿。主管分不清哪份在先，名字没改。}
# en: Let it go and work faster
opt.right.label [1f0a6c] = 算了，干得更快些
# en: {You say nothing and do the next one twice as well, in ink that's hard to copy. It doesn't feel like justice. It feels like work.|You let it go. You write your name on every page from then on, small, in the corner.|You take your notes home. The next piece of work never leaves your sight until it's on the supervisor's desk.}
opt.right.say.1 [d7ade9] = {你什么也没说，把下一份做得加倍好，用难以仿写的墨水。这感觉不像公道。这感觉像干活。|你算了。从那以后，你在每一页的角落里都写上自己的名字，小小的。|你把笔记带回了住处。下一份活儿，在放上主管的桌子之前，一刻也没离开过你的视线。}

@event intern_city_evening
# en: An Evening Off
title [6fa683] = 休息的夜晚
# en: {{member(intern_expedition) or member(intern_field_station): The other interns are going out tonight, three miles to a village dance, with a fiddler and a supper laid on at a few coins a head.|The other interns are going out tonight, to an inn with music and a stall that sells fried bread at midnight.}|Another evening off, and the others are already at the door.|"Coming?" says the intern with the biscuits. "Last time you said next time."} {member(intern_expedition) or member(intern_field_station): {The track is dark, but somebody has a lantern.|It's the only dance for thirty miles.|Someone has brought a fiddle of their own.}|{The streets are bright.|There's a fair on the river.|Somebody knows a band.}} Your work for tomorrow isn't done.
text [a6fa73] = {{member(intern_expedition) or member(intern_field_station): 其他实习生今晚要出去，走三英里去村里的舞会，有提琴手，还有几个钱一位的晚饭。|其他实习生今晚要出去，去一家有音乐的客栈，还有个半夜卖炸面包的小摊。}|又一个休息的夜晚，其他人已经站在门口了。|“去吗？”带饼干的那个实习生说，“上次你说下次。”}{member(intern_expedition) or member(intern_field_station): {小路很黑，好在有人带了灯笼。|这是方圆三十英里唯一的舞会。|有人自己带了把小提琴。}|{街道灯火通明。|河上有个集市。|有人认识一支乐队。}}你明天的活儿还没干完。
# en: A lamplit street far from the academy, interns spilling out of a busy inn, one looking back at the lit window of the workplace.
scene [9f0bec] = 远离学院的一条灯火通明的街道，实习生们从热闹的客栈里涌出来，其中一个回头望着工作地点亮着灯的窗户。
# en: Go out with them
opt.left.label [e99515] = 和他们一起去
# en: {You pay your share of the supper, dance badly, laugh well and walk home at two in the morning, arm in arm with people you met last month. Tomorrow's work is a little worse for it.|You go, and stand your round. You learn more about the place from the other interns in one evening than from a month of briefings, and remember half of it.|You keep last time's promise and go. The intern with the biscuits shares them on the walk home, and tomorrow's work is a little worse for it.}
opt.left.say.1 [89a4dc] = {你付了自己那份晚饭钱，跳舞跳得很糟，笑得很开心，凌晨两点和上个月才认识的人挽着胳膊走回家。明天的活儿因此差了一点。|你去了，还请了一轮。一个晚上从其他实习生那里了解到的东西，比一个月的晨会还多，虽然只记住了一半。|你兑现了上次的承诺，去了。带饼干的那个实习生在回去的路上分给你吃，明天的活儿因此差了一点。}
# en: Finish tomorrow's work
opt.right.label [2c6920] = 干完明天的活
# en: {You finish the work by lamplight. You hear them come home, singing. In the morning your work is the best on the table.|You stay in. The work is good. The evening is long.|"Next time," you say again, and mean it less. Your work is excellent, and the biscuits are gone by morning.}
opt.right.say.1 [07633f] = {你在灯下干完了活。你听见他们唱着歌回来。早上，你的成果是桌上最好的。|你留了下来。活儿干得很好。夜晚很长。|“下次吧，”你又说了一遍，这回没那么真心。你的活儿干得很出色，饼干到早上已经没了。}

@event intern_letter_from_campus
# en: A Letter From the Castle
title [ffb8b9] = 城堡来信
# en: {A letter from {friend}, forwarded twice, with the castle drawn in the margins.|Another letter from campus, this one from {friend}.|{friend}'s handwriting on the envelope. You open it before your coat is off.} {The letter misses you, in a roundabout way.|{They} {are} bored without you, {they} say{s}.|There's gossip, and a pressed flower.} Answering it properly would take the evening.
text [890ed9] = {一封{friend}的信，转寄了两次，页边画着城堡。|又一封来自学院的信，这次是{friend}写的。|信封上是{friend}的字迹。你外套还没脱就拆开了。}{这封信拐弯抹角地说想你。|{They}说没有你很无聊。|里面有八卦，还有一朵压干的花。}好好回信得花一个晚上。
# en: A letter open on a desk far from the academy, its margins full of little drawings of the castle, a student smiling at it.
scene [f98846] = 远离学院的一张桌上摊着一封信，页边画满了城堡的小插画，一个学生对着它微笑。
# en: Write back at length
opt.left.label [7bb28c] = 长长地回一封
# en: {Six pages, with drawings of your own. You post it at dawn and are late for the briefing, and don't mind.|You write back everything: the work, the place, the interns. It's like talking to {them}.|You answer the gossip with gossip of your own, and press a flower from here to send back. It's like being in two places.}
opt.left.say.1 [d15588] = {六页纸，还配了你自己画的插图。你天亮时寄出，晨会迟到了，也不在乎。|你把一切都写了回去：工作、这个地方、实习生们。就像在和{them}说话。|你用自己这边的八卦回应那边的八卦，还压了一朵这里的花寄回去。就像同时身在两处。}
# en: Send a quick note
opt.right.label [40b631] = 回一张短笺
# en: {"Busy. Miss you. More soon." It's true, and it's thin, and you know it.|Three lines and a promise. You mean to write more. The summer is very full.|A quick note, and the pressed flower kept in your notebook. You'll write properly when the summer's less full.}
opt.right.say.1 [2d0d0f] = {“忙。想你。回头细说。”是真话，很单薄，你自己也知道。|三行字和一个承诺。你本想多写一些。这个夏天太满了。|一张短笺，那朵压花夹进了你的笔记本。等夏天没这么满了，你再好好写。}

@event intern_conclave_your_ward
# en: A Ward of Your Own
title [dbf01a] = 属于你的护界
# en: The Conclave is testing a new ward, and the researcher who designed it is ill. "You've read every note," says your supervisor. "Cast it. If it holds, it's yours to keep, and your name goes in the paper." Behind the glass, half the Conclave has come to watch.
text [7343f4] = 七塔议会在测试一种新的护界，设计它的研究员病了。“每一条笔记你都读过，”你的主管说，“施放它。如果它撑住了，就归你了，你的名字也会登上论文。”玻璃后面，半个议会的人都来看了。
# en: A circular test chamber, a student at the centre holding up a shimmering ward against a bolt of light, researchers behind thick glass on their feet.
scene [9c1957] = 一间圆形的测试室，一个学生站在中央，举起一道闪烁的护界挡住一束光，厚玻璃后面的研究员们都站了起来。
# en: Cast it
opt.left.label [e73317] = 施放它
# en: The bolt hits the ward and stops, humming, an inch from your nose. Behind the glass, someone starts clapping. Your name goes in the paper, third of four, and the ward is yours for good.
opt.left.say.1 [a78dfe] = 光束击中护界停了下来，嗡嗡作响，离你的鼻尖只有一寸。玻璃后面有人开始鼓掌。你的名字登上了论文，四位作者中的第三位，而这道护界从此永远属于你。
# en: The ward holds for half a heartbeat and then doesn't. You wake on the floor with your hair standing up and a researcher fanning you with your own notes.
opt.left.say.2 [aa069c] = 护界撑了半个心跳，然后没撑住。你在地板上醒来，头发竖着，一个研究员正拿你自己的笔记给你扇风。
# en: Ask them to wait for the designer
opt.right.label [03931f] = 请他们等设计者回来
# en: "Sensible," says your supervisor, in a voice that means "disappointing". The designer recovers, casts it, and thanks you in the paper's footnotes for the notes you kept.
opt.right.say.1 [4dc945] = “明智，”你的主管说，语气的意思是“令人失望”。设计者康复后施放了它，并在论文的脚注里感谢你保存的笔记。

@event intern_alchemists_safety
# en: The Cracked Vat
title [177790] = 裂开的大桶
# en: The seventh vat at the Guild works has a crack in it. Everyone knows. The foreman says it'll last the season, and the season's quota depends on it. Workers walk past it without looking. You've seen what the steam does to brass.
text [7b9994] = 公会工坊的第七口大桶裂了。人人都知道。工头说它能撑过这一季，这一季的定额全指望它。工人们从旁边走过，看都不看。你见过那蒸汽对黄铜做了什么。
# en: A huge iron vat in an alchemical works, a hairline crack weeping green steam, workers walking past it without looking.
scene [ddd11a] = 炼金工坊里一口巨大的铁桶，一道细缝正渗出绿色的蒸汽，工人们从旁边走过，看都不看。
# en: Report it to the Guild masters
opt.left.label [0fdc16] = 报告给公会长老
# en: The masters close the seventh vat for a week and the foreman doesn't speak to you again. In the third week the replacement vat arrives, and an old worker shakes your hand without a word.
opt.left.say.1 [cd1d6c] = 长老们把第七口桶关停了一个星期，工头从此再没和你说过话。第三个星期，替换的桶运到了，一位老工人一言不发地和你握了握手。
# en: Mend it yourself, quietly
opt.right.label [b83056] = 自己悄悄修好
# en: You seal it from the inside in the night, with a sealant of your own. It holds through the season. The foreman never knows. The old worker does, somehow, and leaves an apple on your bench every morning.
opt.right.say.1 [b14f13] = 你在夜里从内部用自己调的密封剂把它封好。它撑过了这一季。工头始终不知道。那位老工人不知怎么知道了，每天早上在你的工作台上放一个苹果。
# en: The steam gets you as the seal gives. You wake in the works infirmary with blistered hands, and the vat is closed anyway.
opt.right.say.2 [e799fa] = 密封失效时蒸汽扑到了你身上。你在工坊的医务室里醒来，双手起了水泡，那口桶还是被关停了。

@event intern_expedition_new_star
# en: A Star Nobody Charted
title [6ddf06] = 无人记录的星
# en: The lead gives you tonight's watch at the eyepiece, alone. At three in the morning there's a star in it that isn't on any chart: small, steady, blue. The expedition lead is asleep. By custom, whoever records a new star first may name it.
text [bf4e99] = 队长把今晚目镜前的值班交给了你一个人。凌晨三点，目镜里出现了一颗任何星图上都没有的星：小小的，稳定的，蓝色的。考察队长在睡觉。按照惯例，第一个记录新星的人可以为它命名。
# en: A telescope on a high plateau at night, a student with an eye to the eyepiece and a chart on their knee, a single new star circled in red.
scene [c44b5d] = 高原上夜色中的一架望远镜，一个学生一只眼贴着目镜，膝上放着星图，一颗新星被红笔圈了出来。
# en: Wake the lead and share it
opt.left.label [5148ef] = 叫醒队长一起分享
# en: The lead comes in a nightshirt and stares until dawn. The star goes in the record under the expedition's name and yours, and the whole camp toasts it at breakfast.
opt.left.say.1 [9a791d] = 队长穿着睡衣赶来，一直盯到天亮。这颗星以考察队和你的名义记入了记录，全营地在早饭时为它干杯。
# en: Record it in your own name
opt.right.label [43c352] = 以你自己的名字记录
# en: You write it into the log: the time, the place, a name you choose. It's yours for as long as there are charts. At breakfast the lead reads the log twice, and is polite to you all week, which is worse.
opt.right.say.1 [b9bb49] = 你把它写进日志：时间、位置，还有一个你挑的名字。只要星图还在，它就是你的。早饭时队长把日志读了两遍，接下来一个星期都对你很客气，这更糟。

@event intern_field_station_foal
# en: The Orphaned Foal
title [5085db] = 失去母亲的幼驹
# en: On the moor, a hippogriff foal, newborn and alone. The station's rule is plain: you count wild creatures, you don't raise them. The station chief says it won't last the night. It looks at you as if you were the only warm thing on the moor, which you are.
text [ed8dba] = 荒原上有一只鹰头马身有翼兽的幼驹，刚出生，孤零零的。站里的规矩很明确：野生动物只数不养。站长说它活不过今晚。它看着你，好像你是荒原上唯一温暖的东西，而你确实是。
# en: A newborn hippogriff foal shivering in the heather on the moor, a student kneeling with a blanket, the field station lamps far off.
scene [7b4dbb] = 一只刚出生的鹰头马身有翼兽幼驹在荒原的石楠丛中发抖，一个学生拿着毯子跪在一旁，观察站的灯光远在天边。
# en: Take it back and raise it
opt.left.label [f031dc] = 带回去养大
# en: You feed it every two hours for a month and break the rule every one of them. By summer's end it flies. Back at Lumenhold, Professor Brask hears the story and invites you to supper. "Rules," she says, "are for people who've never held a foal."
opt.left.say.1 [df3e67] = 你每两个小时喂它一次，喂了一个月，每一次都在违反规矩。到夏末，它能飞了。回到流明堡，布拉斯克教授听说了这件事，请你吃晚饭。“规矩，”她说，“是给从没抱过幼驹的人定的。”
# en: Count it and leave it
opt.right.label [16751c] = 记下它，然后离开
# en: You write it down: one foal, alone, the date. You don't sleep. In the morning the chief tells you its mother came back in the night. You never find out if that's true.
opt.right.say.1 [fc1a21] = 你把它记了下来：一只幼驹，孤零零的，日期。你没睡着。第二天早上站长告诉你，它的母亲夜里回来了。你永远不知道这是不是真的。

@event intern_thornwick_offer
# en: An Offer From Thornwick
title [ca717f] = 荆木学院的邀请
# en: Thornwick's dean asks to see you on your last week. "Transfer to us," she says, sliding a sealed offer across the desk. "Full scholarship, your own lab bench, a seat in our illusion faculty in time. Lumenhold never valued glamour. We do." She's sincere, and that's the danger.
text [545e64] = 荆木学院的院长在你最后一个星期请你去见她。“转学到我们这儿来，”她说着把一份封好的录取书推过桌面。“全额奖学金，你自己的实验台，将来幻术系的一个教席。流明堡从不看重魅影。我们看重。”她是真诚的，这正是危险所在。
# en: A lacquered office at a rival academy, a smiling dean sliding a sealed offer across a desk, a window full of unfamiliar towers.
scene [6db64f] = 对手学院一间上了漆的办公室，一位微笑的院长把一份封好的录取书推过桌面，窗外满是陌生的塔楼。
# en: Decline, warmly
opt.left.label [1a38c7] = 热情地谢绝
# en: "Lumenhold is home," you say. She smiles as if she expected it. "The offer stands." Back at the castle, Professor Vey hears about it somehow and gives you an approving look that lasts all term.
opt.left.say.1 [00f1eb] = “流明堡是我的家，”你说。她笑了，好像早料到了。“邀请一直有效。”回到城堡，维伊教授不知怎么听说了，给了你一个赞许的眼神，持续了整整一个学期。
# en: Keep the offer, unopened
opt.right.label [a4e05b] = 收下邀请，不拆开
# en: You keep it, sealed, in the bottom of your trunk. Thornwick sends a stipend "as a courtesy". Knowing there's a door out makes some evenings easier, and some harder.
opt.right.say.1 [25475a] = 你把它封着收在箱底。荆木学院寄来一笔津贴，“聊表心意”。知道有一扇退路的门，让有些夜晚好过一些，也让有些夜晚更难熬。

@event intern_unseen_office_file
# en: The File With Your Name
title [725538] = 写着你名字的档案
# en: Sorting files for the Office, you find one with your name on it. It's thin. The clerk has gone to lunch. The last page is about Lumenhold, and the lake, and a tower nobody has opened in a century.
text [273c79] = 替署里整理档案时，你发现一份写着你名字的档案。很薄。文书吃午饭去了。最后一页写的是流明堡、那座湖，还有一座一百年没人打开过的塔。
# en: A windowless office lined with drawers, a student holding open a thin file with their own name on the label, a clerk's empty chair behind them.
scene [210c9d] = 一间没有窗户、四壁都是抽屉的办公室，一个学生翻开一份标签上写着自己名字的薄档案，身后是文书空着的椅子。
# en: Read it all
opt.left.label [f23585] = 全部读完
# en: They know where you sleep and what you eat, which is unsettling. The last page is mostly blacked out. What's left says the seventh tower "is to remain closed", and nothing about why. When the clerk comes back you are filing something else. The clerk looks at you a little too long.
opt.left.say.1 [9882d7] = 他们知道你睡在哪儿、吃些什么，这让人不安。最后一页大半被涂黑了。剩下的部分只说第七塔“应保持封闭”，没说为什么。文书回来时，你正在整理别的东西。文书看你的时间稍微长了一点。
# en: Put it back unread
opt.right.label [154115] = 不看，放回去
# en: You put it back. The clerk returns, checks the drawer and smiles for the first time all summer. "The Office notices who doesn't look," the clerk says. You didn't look. You'll wonder for years.
opt.right.say.1 [4506c9] = 你把它放了回去。文书回来，检查了抽屉，这个夏天第一次露出了笑容。“署里会注意到谁不看，”文书说。你没有看。你会为此纳闷好多年。
